# The classtypes the lab's own rules use, and nothing else.
#
# Suricata reads this to map a rule's `classtype` to a printable category and a priority.
# The image ships its own copy, but it is not readable by the unprivileged user Suricata
# drops to, so the lab carries the two lines it actually needs. Keeping the file here also
# means the lab's alert categories are defined in this repository rather than inherited.
#
# config classification: shortname,short description,priority
config classification: not-suspicious,Not Suspicious Traffic,3
config classification: attempted-recon,Attempted Information Leak,2
